### Create new employee
POST {{WebApiDemo_HostAddress}}/api/employee/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "Afan@123",
  "confirmPassword": "Afan@123"
}
###

POST {{WebApiDemo_HostAddress}}/api/employee/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "Afan@123",
  "confirmPassword": "Afan@456"
}


### Register - triggers BadRequestException
POST {{WebApiDemo_HostAddress}}/api/employee/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "Password1@",
  "confirmPassword": "Password1@"
}


### Create new employee
POST {{WebApiDemo_HostAddress}}/api/employee
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Afan",
  "department": "IT",
  "age": 25,
  "email": "afan@gmail.com",
  "phone": "9876543210"
}
### Update employee
PUT {{WebApiDemo_HostAddress}}/api/employee/13
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Afan Updated",
  "department": "Development",
  "age": 25,
  "email": "afan@gmail.com",
  "phone": "9876543210"
}
###

### Delete employee
DELETE {{WebApiDemo_HostAddress}}/api/employee/8



### LINQ: Get employees by department
GET {{WebApiDemo_HostAddress}}/api/employee/department/IT
Accept: application/json

###

### LINQ: Get employees sorted by name
GET {{WebApiDemo_HostAddress}}/api/employee/sorted
Accept: application/json

###

### LINQ: Get only employee names
GET {{WebApiDemo_HostAddress}}/api/employee/names
Accept: application/json

###

### LINQ: Get total count
GET {{WebApiDemo_HostAddress}}/api/employee/count
Accept: application/json